title: Relay connector multi-connect still causes 429 storms on shared hosts
updated_at: "2026-07-15T15:01:47Z"
---
Dogfood follow-up to existing B200 and B201. GitHub issue: https://github.com/clankercode/c2c/issues/4. On host 3d08761ae3f3 with c2c 0.12.0 5faddd4b, multiple independent c2c relay connect processes were live, including bare and all-brokers forms. Relay inbox peeks repeatedly returned HTTP 429 and flapped into timeouts. Existing singleton and historical-registration mitigations did not prevent the observed multi-connect state. Investigate current process ownership, startup/restart coordination, and doctor/whoami detection. Acceptance: one host-level connector or safe coordination; duplicate connectors are prevented or clearly surfaced; 429 backoff is bounded and does not create an agent-wide receive storm.